  {
    "sha": "864a0fb8bdf309b4091dc8be52fe523a1affe6c9",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDg2NGEwZmI4YmRmMzA5YjQwOTFkYzhiZTUyZmU1MjNhMWFmZmU2Yzk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T17:23:13Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-09T17:23:13Z"
      },
      "message": "Merge upstream/main (70c261ba) into issue/388-per-setup-mount-v2\n\nBrings in #464 (fixture-law gaps), #462/#404 (carry-machine check) and\n#470 (MCP setup/machine/fixture tools).\n\nConflict resolutions:\n- crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs carry_turn: main (#404) checks the\n  two setups share one machine (one_machine -> CARRY_MACHINE_CHANGE_\n  REFUSAL, each setup's own machine via setup_mount::machine_of) and then\n  gates that machine's kind; #388 required both ends to be mills via\n  kind_of_setup. One shared machine has one kind, so main's check covers\n  #388's both-ends rule and is stricter: a carry between two different\n  mills (allowed by #388 alone) now refuses. Kept main's code with a\n  comment naming both laws.\n- crates/app/src/posting.rs fixture_findings: kept main's (#181/#470)\n  Result<FixtureFindings> walk with (name, hit) pairs and the unjudged\n  list, with #388's per-op spindle housing (spindle_of(op.setup), its own\n  machine's) in place of main's active-machine spindle.\n- Semantic (compile) conflict: #470's MCP tools called\n  fixture::table_box(world), which #388 made per setup context. The\n  workholding view now passes each setup context; set_setup_machine\n  reports the table of the machine it names (the setup's own or the\n  document's) via the new fixture::table_of(&Machine), split out of\n  table_box with no change to table_box's result.\n\nRecorded in docs/decisions/388-per-setup-mount.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
